WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.367
-Our next guest
is one of my favorites.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.067
He has his comedy special,

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:07.033
"The Attractives" available
now on YouTube

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.901
and it's probably going
to crack a million tonight.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:12.801
Please welcome the very funny
Mike Vecchione, everybody.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:19.200
♪♪

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.501
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:21.901
-Thank you, guys.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.167
Thank you.
I'm sorry.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.400
I look like every cop that's
been in trouble on the news.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.334
I'm actually a very nice person.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.767
Pandemic was tough.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.334
Height of the pandemic,
my friend calls me.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:37.701
He's like, "Mike,
do you want to go to Spain

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.567
this year for running
with the bulls?"

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:40.734
-Whoo!

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.567
-I go,
"Isn't it a little bit soon?

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.334
Remember last week
when the air almost killed us?

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:50.234
Remember five days ago we were
almost murdered by the air?

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:53.033
Now you want to go
running with the bulls,

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.400
which I know
that's what it's called,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.234
but that's not actually
what you're going to be doing.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:01:01.334
Running with the bulls implies
that the bulls have accepted you

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:04.000
and you guys have decided
to exercise together."

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.400
"What you're going to be doing
is running from the bulls.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.601
Do you understand the
difference?

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.300
Running with? Running from?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.334
Everyone's so focused on
pronouns now.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.234
Maybe we should look at
some of these prepositions.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.400
Thank you.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.167
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.434
You guys are great.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.434
I had bedbugs recently.

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:30.934
And bedbugs are unique
because they attack you

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:35.300
and attack you and attack you
until you break your lease.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:39.501
There's no way to stop bedbugs.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.667
I did figure out a way
to slow them down, though.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.133
I introduced ladybugs
into my apartment.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.667
Now the ladybugs
don't kill the bedbugs,

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.667
but they wear them down
emotionally.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:52.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:54.501
Thank you.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.167
Living with my girl
and it's going pretty good.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.033
I did make a mistake.
We're laying in bed one night.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.701
I go, "Let's get to know
each other a little bit better.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:11.901
On the count of three,
let's blurt out our IQs."

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:15.334
Never do that
with your significant partner.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:18.000
One of you is dumber.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.734
In our case, it was me.
And I was much dumber.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:28.467
Shockingly dumber to the point
where she saw it affected me.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.534
And she tried to save it.
You know, she loves me.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:33.734
She goes, "Mike, you have
a much lower IQ than I do.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.534
Even you're smart enough
to know that."

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:39.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.000
"But you have this other thing
called emotional intelligence,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.300
and that's pretty valuable,
too."

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.834
And I did some research,

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:49.634
and it turns out emotional
intelligence is completely fake.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.434
It's just something that
smart people tell dumb people.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:58.234
"You have this" so that
the dumb people don't feel sad.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.667
And they have to do the jobs

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.767
that the smarter people
don't want to do.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:08.901
As a result, my jobs
in the apartment are as follows.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.868
Sanitation and extermination.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.901
Bugs and trash.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.133
That's my jobs. Bugs and trash.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.834
And sometimes she'll quiz me.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.100
She'll go, "What are your jobs?"

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.501
I'll go, "Bugs and trash."

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.334
And she'll be like,
"Who's my guy?"

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:25.667
I go, "I am."

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:30.067
Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.334
We had an incident
the other day.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.133
There was a bug
in the bathroom.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.000
And the reason I know there
was a bug in the bathroom

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.067
is because she was in the
bathroom and she starts going,

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.868
"A bug, a bug. It's a bug.
There's a bug."

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:46.334
I'm like, "Alright, car alarm,
I got it."

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:48.934
I go hit the light,
bug freezes, I freeze.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.968
It's a standoff.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.634
And I try to kill
this bug three times.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.200
The last time
I stepped directly on him,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.734
scoop him up with toilet paper.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.601
He's wounded, but not dead.
I throw him in the toilet.

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.167
I flush.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:05.100
This bug stiff-arms
the toilet paper.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.701
He Heismans the toilet paper,
gets to the side of the bowl,

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:11.033
wounded, starts climbing out.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:15.367
I see that. I back
out of the bathroom.

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:18.667
I yell at her.
I go, "It's all clear, babe."

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.434
She goes in the bathroom.
She pops back out.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:23.601
She goes, "He's alive and better
than ever."

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:25.868
I go, "Let me tell you
something about this bug.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:29.734
He has more of a will to live
than you and me combined."

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:32.467
She goes, "Well, go back in
there and kill him."

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:35.501
I go, "Relax.
This isn't a Mafia family.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:38.267
You don't just order me to kill.

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.067
This bug has a lot
of the characteristics

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:44.133
that I admire
in any living thing.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:46.334
This bug is mentally tough,

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:49.100
overcomes adversity,
never quits.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.367
This bug is basically
who I want to be as a person."

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:52.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:55.934
"I'm not going to go in there
and kill my role model.

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.367
He just lives with us now."

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.634
She goes, "Well, I'm afraid
to go in the bathroom."

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.367
I go, "Well, you should be

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:05.734
because you ordered
his death three times

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:08.167
and I'm sure he overheard you

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:11.567
because this bug probably
doesn't have the highest IQ,

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:14.000
but I'm sure he's got a lot of
emotional intelligence."

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.834
You guys are the best.
I'm Mike Vecchione.

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:19.534
Thank you!

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.834
-Come on, bud.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.534
Mike Vecchione!

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:27.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:31.634
"The Attractives"
is available now on YouTube.

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.300
We'll be right back, everybody.

